      " RM and increase of ",
      " per upgrade.\n<br>\n<b>Increased cost scaling:</b> Above ",
      " RM, the cost multiplier between purchases increases by an additive\n+",
      " per upgrade. Above ",
      " RM, a new scaling occurs which ignores all the\nprevious behavior. From this point, all upgrades instead behave as if they had an initial cost of ",
      "\nand further upgrade costs increase by ",
